<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Plan 53 §3.2 / §3.3's matrix, CELL R1, under mode `takes-split` (QBX-172).
  Kp, Kc and Km on three tracks of one project, driven through
  `place-recording mode="takes-split"` directly, so the whole case is
  arithmetic: no capture device, no transport, no wall-clock jitter anywhere.

  R1 means the existing child STARTS BEFORE the pass and ENDS INSIDE it
  (`s < a < e <= b`). The rule: cut the child at `a`; the head keeps its own
  span untouched; the piece inside `[a, b)` becomes a column with the old piece
  as take 0 and the pass as take 1, active; the part of the pass no child
  covers becomes a plain cut. A take is then an alternative for exactly the
  span it covers, which is why this mode needs none of §4's take-extent model
  change.

  GEOMETRY, one line, the same on all three lanes. test_sawtooth.wav is 192000
  frames (4 s at 48 kHz), so every number below is a closed form:

      O = [48000, 120000)      the existing child, 72000 frames
      R = [96000, 144000)      the pass, 48000 frames

  so s=48000 < a=96000 < e=120000 < b=144000, and the expected result is

      child 0   plain  [48000,  96000)   the head, srcOffset 0, UNTOUCHED
      child 1   column [96000, 120000)   take 0 = the old piece, take 1 = R
      child 2   plain  [120000,144000)   the tail of the pass, srcOffset 24000
      child 3   does not exist

  INDEX ORDER IS INSERTION ORDER, NOT TIME ORDER, and here they coincide only
  by luck: `split-clip` keeps the HEAD at the operand's index and APPENDS the
  tail, then the trailing plain cut appends after that. The cases for R5 and R6
  are where the two orders genuinely diverge.

  WHY THIS FAILS ON main, and it is worth being exact because the plan
  predicted a different reason. Plan 53's P1 section says `rec_split_r*` fails
  on `main` because "`mode=` is ignored by `readXml`, so the old planner runs
  and the shape is wrong". That was true before M0; since QBX-171 `mode=` is
  read, validated, and `takes-split` is a planner that REFUSES loudly, so on
  `main` the `place-recording` action is REJECTED and the case fails there.
  Both are failures, but only one of them is the one the plan named.

  THE ASSERTIONS STILL DISCRIMINATE THE MODE, which is the part that matters
  and the reason they are not weakened to "the verb succeeded". Were the verb
  ever to fall back to `takes` (`LegacyTakes`), this lane would hold TWO
  children, not three: that planner DROPS a column starting before the pass
  from its plan entirely and places the pass as one plain cut [96000,144000)
  over it, so `0,2` would not resolve and `0,1` would be a plain clip rather
  than a column. A silent fallback is exactly the clean, repeatable false
  finding this project has paid for before, so the shape is what gets checked.

  Km's map is chosen so that BOTH halves of the split say something:

      the map on O is   0:1 ; 24000:0 ; 60000:1        (column frames)
      the split is at column frame 48000 (= a - s)

  so the head must keep `0:1;24000:0` — the two segments below the cut, with
  the one at 60000 TRUNCATED away — and the inside piece's own map, which
  `split-clip` shifts to `0:0;12000:1`, must then be CLEARED by activating the
  pass as a take (QBX-159/B4: a map decides every position, so badging a new
  take without clearing it would badge a take nobody can hear). Those two
  assertions are the whole of "the inside column's map cleared, the tail
  column's map shifted" for this cell; R2, R4 and R6 are where a piece AFTER
  `b` exists and carries a shifted map of its own.

  THE ACTIVE TAKE IS NOT THE MAPPED TAKE on Km, deliberately, for the reason
  comp_map_survives_split.qxa gives at length: an empty map MEANS "ask
  activeTake_", so a case whose active take is the one its map selects passes
  identically against a dropped map.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="rec_split_r1">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <snap-to-grid-disable/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>

    <!-- ============ Kp: a plain clip ============ -->
    <place-clip trackPath="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                timePos="48000" startOffset="0" duration="72000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="48000" duration="72000"
                        startOffset="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="none"/>

    <!-- ============ Kc: a direct column, no comp map ============ -->
    <place-clip trackPath="1" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                timePos="48000" startOffset="0" duration="72000"/>
    <add-take clip="1,0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" startOffset="96000"/>
    <select-take clip="1,0" take="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="1,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="0"
                        comp=""/>

    <!-- ============ Km: a direct column WITH a comp map ============ -->
    <place-clip trackPath="2" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                timePos="48000" startOffset="0" duration="72000"/>
    <add-take clip="2,0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" startOffset="96000"/>
    <!-- select-take CLEARS the map, so it has to come before the segments. -->
    <select-take clip="2,0" take="0"/>
    <set-comp-segment clip="2,0" at="0" take="1"/>
    <set-comp-segment clip="2,0" at="24000" take="0"/>
    <set-comp-segment clip="2,0" at="60000" take="1"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="2,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="0"
                        comp="0:1;24000:0;60000:1"/>

    <!-- ============ THE PASS, same span on every lane ============ -->
    <place-recording trackPath="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     mode="takes-split" timePos="96000" length="48000"/>
    <place-recording trackPath="1" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     mode="takes-split" timePos="96000" length="48000"/>
    <place-recording trackPath="2" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     mode="takes-split" timePos="96000" length="48000"/>

    <!-- ============ Kp ============ -->
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="48000" duration="48000"
                        startOffset="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="none"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,1" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="1"
                        comp=""/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" startTime="96000" duration="24000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,2" startTime="120000" duration="24000"
                        startOffset="24000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,2" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,3" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- ============ Kc: the head keeps its two takes, the inside piece
                     gets a third ============ -->
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,0" startTime="48000" duration="48000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="1,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="0"
                        comp=""/>
    <assert-take-column clip="1,1" shape="direct" takes="3" activeTake="2"
                        comp=""/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,1" startTime="96000" duration="24000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,2" startTime="120000" duration="24000"
                        startOffset="24000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,3" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- ============ Km: the head's map TRUNCATED, the inside piece's
                     map CLEARED by the activation ============ -->
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,0" startTime="48000" duration="48000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="2,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="0"
                        comp="0:1;24000:0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="2,1" shape="direct" takes="3" activeTake="2"
                        comp=""/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,1" startTime="96000" duration="24000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,2" startTime="120000" duration="24000"
                        startOffset="24000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,3" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- ONE UNDO PER PASS puts each lane back exactly as it was: the whole
         plan is one composite, so one entry per `place-recording`. -->
    <undo count="3"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="48000" duration="72000"
                        startOffset="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="1,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="0"
                        comp=""/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,0" startTime="48000" duration="72000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,1" expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="2,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="0"
                        comp="0:1;24000:0;60000:1"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,0" startTime="48000" duration="72000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,1" expectReject="true"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="3"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
